Under the second milestone, recoveries that may be deducted from the payment due include:  
- amounts on account of short supply of goods;  
- liquidated damages for delay in supply;  
- liquidated damages (or other recoveries) related to installation, testing and commissioning activities.  

(Procurement of Goods Manual, p. 83)

Missing pages or illegible documents can be overlooked only when they qualify as minor irregularities that do not alter the substantive bid requirements, incur no financial consequence, and leave the tenderers’ relative ranking unchanged. Specifically, such issues may be waived if they:

- Do not constitute a material deviation from the bid specifications;  
- Have no financial impact on the procurement;  
- Do not prejudice or affect the ranking order of the tenderers.  

When these conditions are satisfied, the procuring entity may seek clarification from the bidder; failure to respond appropriately can result in tender rejection.  

(Procurement of Goods Manual, p. 119)

